{"path":"container/unordered_set/count","title":"std::unordered_set<Key,Hash,KeyEqual,Allocator>::count","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::unordered_set&lt;Key,Hash,KeyEqual,Allocator&gt;::</span>count","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/unordered_set/count","section":"container","kind":"page","summary":"Constant on average, worst case linear in the size of the container.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx11\" id=\"Version_1\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">size_type count<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> Key<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> key <span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (1) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(since C++11)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx20\" id=\"Version_2\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> K <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br>size_type count<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> K<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> x <span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (2) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(since C++20)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1)</span> Returns the number of elements with key that compares equal to the specified argument <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">key</span></code>, which is either <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">​<span class=\"nu0\">0</span>​</span></code> or <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"nu0\">1</span></span></code> since this container does not allow duplicates.</div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">2)</span> Returns the number of elements with key that compares equivalent to the specified argument <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">x</span></code>. This overload participates in overload resolution only if <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">Hash<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">is_transparent</span></span></code> and <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">KeyEqual<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">is_transparent</span></span></code> are valid and each denotes a type. This assumes that such <code>Hash</code> is callable with both <code>K</code> and <code>Key</code> type, and that the <code>KeyEqual</code> is transparent, which, together, allows calling this function without constructing an instance of <code>Key</code>.</div>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> key\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> key value of the elements to count\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> x\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> a value of any type that can be transparently compared with a key\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1)</span> Number of elements with key <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">key</span></code>, that is either <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"nu0\">1</span></span></code> or <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">​<span class=\"nu0\">0</span>​</span></code>.</div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">2)</span> Number of elements with key that compares equivalent to <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">x</span></code>.</div>\n<h3 id=\"Complexity\">Complexity</h3>\n<p>Constant on average, worst case linear in the size of the container.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<table class=\"wikitable ftm-begin ftm-has-value\">\n<tr>\n<th><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/feature_test\">Feature-test</a> macro</th>\n<th><abbr>Value</abbr></th>\n<th><abbr>Std</abbr></th>\n<th>Feature\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/w/cpp/feature_test#cpp_lib_generic_unordered_lookup\"><code>__cpp_lib_generic_unordered_lookup</code></a></td>\n<td><a href=\"/w/cpp/compiler_support/20#cpp_lib_generic_unordered_lookup_201811L\"><code>201811L</code></a></td>\n<td><span class=\"t-mark\">(C++20)</span></td>\n<td>Heterogeneous comparison lookup in <a href=\"/w/cpp/container#Unordered_associative_containers\">unordered associative containers</a>, overload <span class=\"t-v\">(2)</span>\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;algorithm&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;unordered_set&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/container/unordered_set\"><span class=\"kw1297\">std::<span class=\"me2\">unordered_set</span></span></a> set<span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"nu0\">2</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">7</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">1</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">8</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">2</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">8</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">1</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">8</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">2</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">8</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"The set is: \"</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">for</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">int</span> e <span class=\"sy4\">:</span> set<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> e <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">' '</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <span class=\"kw4\">auto</span> <span class=\"br0\">[</span>min, max<span class=\"br0\">]</span> <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/algorithm/ranges/minmax\"><span class=\"kw3030\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">minmax</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>set<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>Numbers from \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> min <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\" to \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> max <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\" that are in the set: \"</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">for</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">int</span> i<span class=\"br0\">{</span>min<span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> i <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;=</span> max<span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"sy2\">++</span>i<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n        <span class=\"kw1\">if</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span>set.<span class=\"me1\">count</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>i<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <span class=\"nu0\">1</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n            <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> i <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">' '</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Possible output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>The set is: 8 1 7 2\nNumbers from 1 to 8 that are in the set: 1 2 7 8</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/container/unordered_set/find\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>find</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  finds element with specific key <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/container/unordered_set/contains\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>contains</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(C++20)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  checks if the container contains element with specific key <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/container/unordered_set/equal_range\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>equal_range</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  returns range of elements matching a specific key <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Complexity","id":"Complexity"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"container","title":"Containers library"},{"path":"container/unordered_set","title":"std::unordered_set"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::unordered_set<Key,Hash,KeyEqual,Allocator>::count","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"2 declarations; revisions: since C++11, since C++20. Returns the number of elements with key that compares equal to the specified argument key, which is…"},{"label":"Parameters","note":"key, x"},{"label":"Return value","note":"Number of elements with key key, that is either 1 or 0 ."},{"label":"Complexity","note":"Constant on average, worst case linear in the size of the container."},{"label":"Notes"},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"find","note":"finds element with specific key"},{"label":"contains","note":"checks if the container contains element with specific key"},{"label":"equal_range","note":"returns range of elements matching a specific key"}]}]},"standards":["C++11","C++20"],"wordCount":345,"codeBlockCount":2}
